{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gold-aciduric-vireo","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Config-driven priority mapping + per-project create_defaults\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nPriority mapping is hardcoded (`value_maps.LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA`), and issue creation\nsupplies no project-configurable default fields. Two related gaps: (1) a Jira project with\na different priority scheme (renamed or fewer levels) can't remap rebar's 0–4 priorities;\n(2) creating an issue in a project that **requires** fields beyond Project/Reporter/Summary\n(discovered via createmeta in the live PoC) has no place to declare echo-safe default\nvalues, so creation fails. Both become config-driven on the S1 core: a `priority_map`\naxis and a per-project `create_defaults` block.\n\n## Approach\n\nWire two S1 axes. **Priority:** resolve the effective priority map over the built-in\ndefault (`LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA`); an unmapped priority drifts (priority is a soft field —\nleave Jira's value, warn) rather than failing the whole sync. **create_defaults:** a\nper-project table of `field → value` applied only at issue-create time to satisfy the\nproject's required-create fields (the createmeta-declared requireds); values are static\nconfig (no guessing), and are echo-safe because they are write-only-on-create and not\nreconciled thereafter. Validation (S1) fails closed if a `priority_map` value is outside\nthe declared priority vocabulary when one is declared.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py` — priority\n  built-in default becomes injected fallback.\n- The issue-create path in the reconciler outbound (create payload assembly) — merge\n  `create_defaults` into the create fields.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_priority_and_create_defaults.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Priority config-effect contrast (unit):** with a `priority_map` override, an outbound\n  ticket targets the overridden Jira priority; default targets the built-in value — same\n  path, different config.\n- **Priority drift (failure path):** an unmapped priority leaves Jira's priority unchanged\n  and warns; asserted on the recorded alert.\n- **create_defaults applied:** with `create_defaults.customfield_x=\"Y\"`, the assembled\n  create payload includes that field with that value; without it, the field is absent —\n  asserted on the create payload.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Effective priority map = built-in ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>`; a non-default\n  overlay changes the outbound priority through the real path — verified by\n  `test_priority_and_create_defaults.py::test_priority_config_effect`.\n- [ ] An unmapped priority drifts with a recorded warning — verified by\n  `test_priority_and_create_defaults.py::test_priority_drifts`.\n- [ ] `create_defaults` fields are merged into the create payload per project — verified by\n  `test_priority_and_create_defaults.py::test_create_defaults_applied`.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit** — priority resolution and create-payload assembly are pure\nfunctions; oracles are the produced priority field, the recorded alert, and the assembled\ncreate payload.","id":"a881-2d9a-16bf-4acb","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Config-driven priority mapping + per-project create_defaults"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787290322182811001,"uuid":"0cb54fd9-ec3a-4621-9a53-2f0c07fc5b61"}